\begin{cases} 
a(1)^2 + b(1) + c = -1 \\
a(2)^2 + b(2) + c = 3 \\
a(-3)^2 + b(-3) + c = 4 
\end{cases}
\]
which simplifies to: \[
\begin{cases} 
a + b + c = -1 \\
4a + 2b + c = 3 \\
9a - 3b + c = 4 
\end{cases}
\]
We can solve this system of equations to find \( a \), \( b \), and \( c \). Subtract the first equation from the second and the second from the third to eliminate \( c \): \[
\begin{cases} 
3a + b = 4 \\
5a - 5b = 1 
\end{cases}
\]
Simplify the second equation by dividing by 5: \[
\begin{cases} 
3a + b = 4 \\
a - b = \frac{1}{5} 
\end{cases}
\]
Adding these two equations gives: \[
4a = \frac{21}{5} \implies a = \frac{21}{20}
\]
Substitute \( a = \frac{21}{20} \) into \( a - b = \frac{1}{5} \): \[
\frac{21}{20} - b = \frac{1}{5} \implies b = \frac{21}{20} - \frac{4}{20} = \frac{17}{20}
\]
Substitute \( a = \frac{21}{20} \) and \( b = \frac{17}{20} \) into \( a + b + c = -1 \): \[
\frac{21}{20} + \frac{17}{20} + c = -1 \implies \frac{38}{20} + c = -1 \implies c = -1 - \frac{38}{20} = -\frac{20}{20} - \frac{38}{20} = -\frac{58}{20} = -\frac{29}{10}
\]
Thus, the remainder polynomial is \( r(x) = \frac{21}{20}x^2 + \frac{17}{20}x - \frac{29}{10} \). To find \( r(6) \): \[
